{%- comment -%}
  Abmira cart footer.

  Deliberately near-empty. Everything a shopper sees - items, warning,
  note, the order ticket and the totals - is rendered by
  sections/main-cart-items.liquid, because the design is a two-column grid
  with a sticky ticket and two sibling Shopify sections cannot be made
  into one grid without wrapping them from the layout.

  What remains is the scaffolding assets/cart.js still reaches for on
  every quantity change. It lists main-cart-footer in getSectionsToRender
  and swaps this section's .js-contents, so both have to exist or the
  update throws part way through and the cart silently stops responding.

  #cart-errors is where cart-wide errors are written.

  Express checkout buttons are gone on purpose, per the cart design.
  content_for_additional_checkout_buttons is what rendered Shop Pay,
  Apple Pay and Google Pay here.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="ab-cart-footer" id="main-cart-footer" data-id="{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="js-contents">
    <p id="cart-errors" class="ab-cart-errors" role="alert"></p>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Cart footer",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The cart's totals, note and checkout button are all in the Cart items section above. This one only carries the plumbing Shopify needs and has nothing to set."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
